bbH_yt2 -- yt^2 component of bb~H production, 4FS, NLO QCD + PS
===============================================================
Code built for LHCHWG studies
======================================

pp -> H b b~ with massive b, restricted to the contribution
proportional to yt^2: the Higgs couples to gluons through the
heavy-top effective vertex and the b quarks come from gluon
splitting. This is the component of arXiv:2307.09992.
Amplitudes come from Recola2 with the HEFT model file.

Differences from bbH4FS
---------------------------
* No bottom Yukawa. The yt^2 contribution has none, so all the
  running-Yukawa machinery of bbH4FS is gone.
* Coupling powers: res_powst = 4, res_powew = 1. In the Recola HEFT
  model the effective Hgg/Hggg/Hgggg vertices carry (QCD,QED) =
  (2,1)/(3,1)/(4,1), so every Born diagram has (4,1). The yb^2 Born
  has (2,1) instead - selecting QCD=4 is what projects onto yt^2 and
  removes both yb^2 and the yb*yt interference.
* Amplitude provider is recola instead of Openloops/Analytic as in yb^2,
  the POWHEG-recola interface has been ported from MiNNLO bblnulnu code.

Building
--------
1. Get Recola2. The distributed package is a small cmake superbuild
   that downloads recola2, COLLIER and the requested model file from
   hepforge at configure time (so the first build needs network):

     wget -O recola2-collier-2.2.4.tar.gz \
       "https://recola.hepforge.org/downloads/?f=recola2-collier-2.2.4.tar.gz"
     tar xzf recola2-collier-2.2.4.tar.gz

   (project page: https://recola.hepforge.org)

2. Build it with the HEFT model file. This is essential: the default
   SM model file has no effective Hgg vertex and the process cannot be
   generated with it.

     cd recola2-collier-2.2.4
     mkdir -p build-heft && cd build-heft
     cmake .. -Dmodel=HEFT -Dstatic=ON \
              -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<your-prefix>
     make -j && make install

3. Point the Makefile at it. Edit the two variables in the block
   marked "SET THESE TWO PATHS" at the top:

     RECOLALOCATION = <your-prefix>
     RECOLASRC      = <path>/recola2-collier-2.2.4/recola2-2.2.4

   RECOLALOCATION is the install prefix (lib/ + include/).
   RECOLASRC is the unpacked source tree: its include/ carries the
   internal modules (globals_rcl) that the install prefix does not
   ship but that recola.f needs.

   Current values in this Makefile:
     RECOLALOCATION = $(HOME)/Packages/recola-heft-install
     RECOLASRC      = $(HOME)/Packages/recola2-collier-2.2.4/recola2-2.2.4

4. LHAPDF and FastJet are found via lhapdf-config / fastjet-config on
   PATH; if they are not there, set LHAPDF_CONFIG / FASTJET_CONFIG in
   the Makefile or on the make command line.

5. make        ("make check_recola" alone verifies the Recola paths)

Running
-------
See powhegrun-benchmark2307.09992/ for a validated card and the
comparison with the paper.

alpha_s is frozen in Recola (the HEFT model file has no
qcd_rescaling, so set_alphas_rcl is refused). The running coupling is
restored exactly in the interface: muMS/muUV/muIR track muR per phase
-space point and the amplitudes are rescaled by
(alphas(muR)/als_frozen)**n, which is exact because they are
homogeneous in alpha_s at fixed muMS. recola_alphas is therefore an
arbitrary normalisation.

powheg.input keys specific to this process
------------------------------------------
  runningscales 4    HT/4 over all final-state particles (eq.3 of
                     2307.09992); 0..3 are the bbH4FS choices
  btlscalereal 1     REQUIRED with runningscales 4: without it POWHEG
                     leaves flg_btildepart='b' and the real
                     contribution uses the Born HT (NLO ~7% too high)
  wilsonlog 1        add the (1/6)log(muR^2/mt^2) term of C1 that the
                     Recola HEFT model does not supply (default on;
                     set 0 to compare with Higgs-Characterisation
                     based numbers)
  recola_alphas      value alpha_s is frozen to (arbitrary)
  recola_muren       reference scale for the freeze
  recola_nfalphas    nf in the alpha_s counterterm dZgs (default
                     st_nlight = 4)
  checkvirtpoles 1   validate the virtual: IR poles against the
                     Casimir prediction, UV finiteness, nf dependence

Validation
----------
  Born vs MG5_aMC LO                 0.2%
  real: soft/collinear limits        -> 1 within 5e-6
  virtual: IR double poles           gg -6.000, qqbar -8/3, to 2e-6
  virtual: UV finiteness             independent of DeltaUV
  full setup vs 2307.09992           LO, NLO agreement
Massification (MAapprox) and virtinborn
---------------------------------------
MAapprox 1 registers, next to the massive processes, the massless image
of each Born channel, g g / q q~ -> H s s~ (d d~ for an s s~ initial
state), with MS = 0 and the massive b kept in the loops, so exact and
approximated amplitudes live in one Recola session. As in
MiNNLOPS_res/ttH_NLO, setvirtual then
  1. maps the massive point onto its massless image,
  2. evaluates at Q = etascfact*sqrt(s_bbH)
         M1M0(Q) = [ 2*F1 + V0/B0 ] * B_massive
     (F1 the Mitov-Moch constant, virtual.f massif_factors),
  3. runs it to muR with the exact one-loop RGE and the poles of the
     MASSIVE amplitude at Q:
         V(muR) = V(Q) + c1 L + c2 L^2/2 + n b0 L B ,  L = log(muR^2/Q^2)
     plus the change of the HEFT Wilson log (wilsonlog).

virtinborn 1 puts the virtual in place of the Born, so a stage 1-4 run
integrates the one-loop contribution alone; run it once with
MAapprox 0 (exact) and once with MAapprox 1, and vary etascfact for the
scale ambiguity of the approximation. Use bornonly 1 + LOevents 1.

Checks against the exact amplitude
  MAflowcheck 1: exact V(Q) run to muR vs exact V(muR) -- agree to
     <1e-3 of V (residual linear in L, scaling like m_b^2, origin not
     identified; independent of the massification).
  MAdebug 2 (fort.78): massified vs exact on the same point. Ratio
     1.0000 for pT_b > 80 GeV, 0.997-1.0007 for 20-80 GeV, a few % low
     below 10 GeV (m_b/pT power corrections).

eta variation: etascfact is a reweighting key (rwl_setup_param_weights_user.f,
common pwhg_MAeta.h), as in ttH_NLO. Stage 4 adds e.g.
  <weight id='11eta2'> renscfact=1.0 facscfact=1.0 etascfact=2.0 </weight>
  <weight id='11etaH'> renscfact=1.0 facscfact=1.0 etascfact=0.5 </weight>
The exact virtual is eta independent.

See ma-test/RESULT.txt for the pointwise validation of F1.
